  "solution": "**Given:**\n\n(300, 100, 100)\n\n(88, 66, 11)\n\n**Logic: **Third no. = [(First no. - Second no.) ÷ 2]\n\n**(300, 100, 100) →**\n\n⇒ [(300 - 100) ÷ 2]\n\n⇒ (200 ÷ 2) = 100\n\n**(88, 66, 11) →**\n\n⇒ [(88 - 66) ÷ 2]\n\n⇒ (22 ÷ 2) = 11\n\nChecking all the given options:\n\n**1.** (60, 40, 20) →\n\n⇒ [(60 - 40) ÷ 2]\n\n⇒ (20 ÷ 2) = 10\n\n**2. **(44, 22, 11) →\n\n⇒ [(44 - 22) ÷ 2]\n\n⇒ (22 ÷ 2) = **11**\n\n**3.** (90, 50, 70) →\n\n⇒ [(90 - 50) ÷ 2]\n\n⇒ (40 ÷ 2) = 20\n\n**4. **(50, 4, 25) →\n\n⇒ [(50 - 4) ÷ 2]\n\n⇒ (46 ÷ 2) = 23\n\nHere, (44, 22, 11) shows a similar relation to the given set of numbers.\n\nHence, the correct answer is \"Option (2)\".",
